id: STYLE-021
ilities: [accessibility]
source: cpm
maturity: 3
action: advisory
title: Non-inclusive terminology (ableist/gendered)
category: inclusivity
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .js .tsx .jsx .py .java .go .cpp .h .rb .cs .sh .md .yml .yaml
  exclude_paths: node_modules/ vendor/ dist/ build/ .git/
patterns:
  - regex: \bsanity check\b
    message: sanity check → use confidence check
  - regex: \bcrazy\b
    message: crazy → use unexpected
  - regex: \binsane\b
    message: insane → use extreme
  - regex: \bcrippled\b
    message: crippled → use degraded
  - regex: \bcripple\b
    message: cripple → use severely limit
  - regex: \blame\b
    message: lame → use weak
  - regex: \bdumb\b
    message: dumb → use simple
  - regex: \bblind spot\b
    message: blind spot → use visibility gap
  - regex: \bman-hours\b
    message: man-hours → use person-hours
  - regex: \bmanpower\b
    message: manpower → use workforce
  - regex: \bmiddleman\b
    message: middleman → use intermediary
  - regex: \bguys\b
    message: guys → use everyone
fix: Replace ableist and gendered terms with inclusive alternatives
